__pycache__
.vscode
.codex
.pytest_cache
dist
# Anchored: an unanchored ``build*`` matches at every depth, so it also
# swallowed src/sweep/build.py -- a shipped module -- silently.
/build/
/build.*
src/sweep/*.so
tests
*.egg-info
*.csv
*.json
test/3drtm
examples/test_figures
examples/multi-gpu/torch/multi_gpu_acoustic_fwi_*/
examples/multi-gpu/jax/multi_gpu_acoustic_fwi_*/
examples/models/models
examples/models/**
!examples/models/
!examples/models/**/
!examples/models/**/*.py
!examples/models/*/README*
!examples/models/**/.gitkeep
test/cuda
test/test_outputs/
test/outputs/
slurm_logs/
dcgm/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored, `scripts/` matches a
# directory at ANY depth, which silently swallowed .github/scripts -- the
# workflow added in this very commit calls a script from there, and `git add`
# only warns when a path is ignored, so the CI would have failed on a missing
# file with nothing in the diff to explain it.
/scripts/
site/
.cache/

# Development scaffolding kept out of a PUBLIC repo.
# Root-level underscore directories are this repo's scratch convention: one-shot
# sbatch/benchmark/debug scripts for a feature under construction. They carry
# cluster-specific absolute paths (/ibex/user/<name>, conda prefixes), which is
# noise for anyone cloning and leaks our directory layout. Keep them local, or
# promote the durable parts into docs/.
/_*/
